description  "STAGED DESIGN SEQUENCE, stage D of four -- THE KINETIC BED. The same loop as stages A-C with the converter as an ADIABATIC plug-flow catalyst bed on the Dyson & Simon (1968) rate law, and the bed VOLUME computed by the engine: a DesignSpec solves V_bed so the effluent is 5 K short of the rate law's own equilibrium (US 5,352,428's per-bed definition, the same source and value stage C imposed), with a preheater landing the loop gas at stage C's 700 K by its own inverse solve. The volume the engine computes sits beside stage C's space-velocity volume, and the per-pass conversion a single adiabatic bed can reach sits beside stage C's isothermal 46.60 % -- both gaps are the lesson.";
verbosity    3;
